id: ops-eyi8
title: The guarded launcher template reads a pm-ops directory without package.json as an omit-dev install and skips the merge drivers
description: "Greptile P2 on pm-slack#117 and pm-starter#115 (2026-09-25), companion hub item pm-cli-website-dqg7. templates/prepare-merge-driver.ts treated MODULE_NOT_FOUND from the pm-ops/package.json probe as proof that pm-ops is absent. A broken install that leaves node_modules/pm-ops as a directory with no package.json, or as a dangling link, fails the probe the same way, so the launcher printed the omit-dev notice, exited 0 and left the clone without merge drivers. The next multi-agent merge would then hard-conflict on tracker files. The fix: an entry at node_modules/pm-ops (lstat, so a dangling link counts) also means present, and the original resolution error is rethrown."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[3]: fail-open,merge-driver,multi-agent
created_at: "2026-09-25T08:58:07.579Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-25T09:09:42.145Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-25T09:09:40.290Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-25T09:09:40.290Z"
author: claude-hub
acceptance_criteria: "A consumer whose node_modules/pm-ops is a directory without package.json, or a dangling link, fails the prepare hook without the skip notice; An absent pm-ops still skips with exactly one notice; Both new fixture cases fail against the previous template"
repro_steps: "1. In a consumer checkout, create node_modules/pm-ops as an empty directory (or a dangling symlink). 2. Run node scripts/prepare-merge-driver.ts (the npm prepare hook). 3. Observe: 'pm-ops is not installed (omit-dev install); skipping merge-driver install', exit 0, no merge.* entries in git config."
resolution: The launcher template fails a broken pm-ops install instead of reading it as an omit-dev install
expected_result: A clone whose node_modules/pm-ops is broken fails the prepare hook; an absent pm-ops still skips with one notice
actual_result: "10/10 launcher fixture cases pass, the two new ones fail on the previous template; release:check exits 0"
